Here's a fully integrated solution for an HTML page that allows users to toggle between a default theme and a "night mode" with smooth transitions and persistent user preferences using **HTML**, **CSS**, and **JavaScript**. The script is designed to be **cross-browser compatible** and stores the user’s preference using `localStorage`.

---

### ✅ Features Implemented

- **Interactive Toggle Button**: A button to switch between themes.
- **Smooth Transitions**: A 0.5-second transition effect for background and text color.
- **Persistent Preference**: User preference is stored using `localStorage` and restored on subsequent visits.
- **Cross-browser Compatibility**: Uses standard APIs (`localStorage`, `classList`, `DOMContentLoaded`), which are supported in all modern browsers.

---

### 📄 Full HTML Code

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
  <title>Theme Toggle Page</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 2rem;
      transition: background-color 0.5s ease, color 0.5s ease;
    }

    body.default-theme {
      background-color: #ffffff;
      color: #000000;
    }

    body.night-mode {
      background-color: #000000;
      color: #ffffff;
    }

    h1, p {
      max-width: 600px;
    }

    button {
      padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      cursor: pointer;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 5px;
      background-color: #444;
      color: #fff;
      transition: background-color 0.3s ease;
    }

    button:hover {
      background-color: #666;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body class="default-theme">
  <h1>Welcome to My Website</h1>
  <p>This is a sample paragraph. You can toggle between the default and night mode using the button below.</p>
  <button id="theme-toggle">Toggle Night Mode</button>

  <script>
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
      const button = document.getElementById('theme-toggle');
      const body = document.body;

      // Load saved theme from localStorage or default to 'default-theme'
      let currentTheme = localStorage.getItem('theme') || 'default-theme';
      applyTheme(currentTheme);

      // Function to apply the theme
      function applyTheme(theme) {
        body.classList.remove('default-theme', 'night-mode');
        body.classList.add(theme);
      }

      // Toggle theme on button click
      button.addEventListener('click', function () {
        currentTheme = currentTheme === 'default-theme' ? 'night-mode' : 'default-theme';
        applyTheme(currentTheme);
        localStorage.setItem('theme', currentTheme);
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### 🧪 How It Works

- **On Page Load**:
  - Checks `localStorage` for the previously selected theme.
  - Applies the stored theme or defaults to `default-theme`.
- **Toggle Button**:
  - Switches the theme by toggling the body class.
  - Updates `localStorage` to remember the user's choice.
- **CSS Transitions**:
  - Ensures a smooth visual transition between themes for a better user experience.

---

### 🛠 Notes

- **Fallback for No JavaScript**: If JavaScript is disabled, the page will default to the light theme and will not support toggling.
- **Scalability**: This pattern can be extended to support more themes or additional styling changes.
- **Accessibility**: You can add `aria-label` or `aria-pressed` to the toggle button to improve accessibility.

---

This solution provides a clean, functional, and user-friendly theme toggle system with persistent preferences and a smooth visual transition, fulfilling all the requirements of the problem.

