To implement a responsive sidebar that collapses and expands automatically with a dropdown menu on smaller screens, follow this solution using **HTML**, **CSS**, and **JavaScript**.

---

### ✅ **Features**
- **Responsive behavior**: The sidebar collapses into a narrow column on small screens.
- **Dropdown menu**: Menu items are displayed as a dropdown when the sidebar is collapsed.
- **Automatic toggle**: The dropdown opens/closes when the screen size changes.

---

### 🧩 **HTML Structure**
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
  <title>Responsive Sidebar</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <div class="sidebar">
    <button id="menuToggle">☰</button>
    <ul class="menu">
      <li><a href="#">Home</a></li>
      <li><a href="#">About</a></li>
      <li><a href="#">Services</a></li>
      <li><a href="#">Contact</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="content">
    <h1>Main Content</h1>
    <p>This is the main content area.</p>
  </div>

  <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### 🎨 **CSS (styles.css)**
```css
/* Base styles */
body {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}

.sidebar {
  width: 200px;
  height: 100vh;
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  background-color: #333;
  color: white;
  transition: width 0.3s;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.menu {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
  padding-top: 20px;
}

.menu li {
  padding: 10px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #555;
}

.menu li a {
  color: white;
  text-decoration: none;
}

#menuToggle {
  display: none;
  width: 100%;
  background: none;
  border: none;
  color: white;
  font-size: 24px;
  padding: 10px;
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Responsive styles */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .sidebar {
    width: 50px;
  }

  .menu {
    display: none;
    position: absolute;
    top: 50px;
    left: 50px;
    background-color: #333;
    width: 150px;
    z-index: 10;
  }

  .sidebar.active .menu {
    display: block;
  }

  #menuToggle {
    display: block;
  }
}

.content {
  margin-left: 200px;
  padding: 20px;
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .content {
    margin-left: 50px;
  }
}
```

---

### 🧠 **JavaScript (script.js)**
```javascript
// Toggle dropdown menu on button click
document.getElementById("menuToggle").addEventListener("click", function () {
  document.querySelector(".sidebar").classList.toggle("active");
});

// Close dropdown when screen is resized to large
window.addEventListener("resize", function () {
  if (window.innerWidth > 768) {
    document.querySelector(".sidebar").classList.remove("active");
  }
});
```

---

### 📱 **How It Works**
- On **large screens**, the sidebar is fully visible with all menu items.
- On **small screens**:
  - The sidebar collapses to a narrow column (`50px`).
  - A hamburger button (`☰`) appears.
  - Clicking the button toggles a dropdown menu (`<ul class="menu">`).
- When the **screen is resized to a larger size**, the dropdown is automatically hidden.

---

### ✅ **Key Considerations**
- **Accessibility**: Add `aria-expanded` and `aria-label` to the toggle button for better screen reader support.
- **Dropdown Positioning**: Uses absolute positioning to display the dropdown outside the narrow sidebar.
- **Transitions**: Smooth width transitions for the sidebar when collapsing/expand.

---

This solution provides a clean, responsive sidebar with a dropdown menu for smaller screens, ensuring a user-friendly experience across all device sizes.

